# Design system (`design/`)

## Sources of truth (read before inventing UI)

1. `design/design.md` — stack, visual DNA, component instructions
2. `design/Design Portfolio Handbook - FLUX.md` — homepage section order and trust strategy
3. `design/Reference1–16` — layout / typography / density references
4. Implemented tokens live in `src/styles/v2.css` (prefer these over outdated hex in older docs)

Do **not** restyle from `vittesh_portfolio_amaterasu_style.md` (sage/emerald) unless the user explicitly asks. Current direction is the red research archive.

## Current visual direction

- Cool gray-blue light surfaces + ink dark; accent `#F23828` / dark `#FF5447`
- Oversized geometric display (Jakarta), Instrument serif for quotes, JetBrains Mono labels (`archive-label`)
- Hairline `border-subtle` rules, four-column research grid, mono indexes (`01`, `↗`, `→`)
- Theme: system default + paper / ink; CSS vars on `.v2-root` / `.v2-root.dark`

## Flux homepage order

Hero → Trust → Why → Work → About → CTA

Prospects must answer quickly: who is this, can I see work, how do I contact.

## When building UI

- Preserve established v2 patterns in `src/components/v2/archive/` and singularity styles
- Use `bg-accent-pop`, `border-border-subtle`, `archive-display` / `archive-serif` / `archive-label` — don’t invent a parallel type scale
- Prefer asymmetrical whitespace and grid lines over card-heavy dashboards
- Case studies: clear problem → approach → outcome; metrics in brackets or bordered blocks
- About portrait: `/assets/images/profile.png` only — never `about.png`
- Live production routes (`/`, `/about`, `/work`) stay untouched; ship preview under `/v2`

## References for craft (not copy-paste themes)

- Amaterasu-level motion craft (scroll reveal, precision cursor) — keep red archive palette
- 21st.dev for primitives when needed
- Niccolò Miranda 404 for playful error/interaction references
